{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-habiro-ring","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:habiro-ring","kind":"definition","title":"Habiro ring $\\widehat{\\mathbb{Z}[q]}$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-algebraic-quantum-volume"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HabiroRing.HabiroElement","text":"habiro-ring.md","leanSource":"habiro-ring.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:habiro-ring\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R = \\mathbb{Z}[q]</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Habiro ring</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widehat{\\mathbb{Z}[q]}_q</code> is the inverse limit of the polynomial rings <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R / ( (q; q)_n )</code> as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\to \\infty</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q; q)_n = \\prod_{k=1}^n (1 - q^k)</code> is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Pochhammer symbol:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\widehat{\\mathbb{Z}[q]}_q\n  \\;:=\\;\n  \\varprojlim_n \\frac{\\mathbb{Z}[q]}{((q; q)_n)}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-ring.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.5.9","page":"b/def-habiro-ring","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.HabiroRing.HabiroElement","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-ring.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
